You can try to use the development version, but I don't think it will help. What experiment are you running? RRBS or WGBS ? updating to development version might help with memory. Also, removing intermediate objects such as methylRawList will help with the memory.

But I can't tell you where this specific error is coming from without more information <http://stackoverflow.com/questions/5963269/how-to-make-a-great-r-reproducible-example>, I guess nobody can. You are not even sharing the most basic information: which functions are you running and which one of them gives the error. Please see the link above if you need more help, without a reproducible example, it is difficult to find what is going wrong, it has to do something with GRanges objects, but many functions use those objects.

Best,
Altuna

